@*
    _OnboardingBanner.cshtml — the M22 onboarding affordance (D5, ADR 0132).

    Rendered in _Layout.cshtml (next to _PinnedAnnouncement / the guest
    notice). It is the dismissible home/nav banner for the guided walk-through:

      - Renders ONLY when the signed-in resident's OnboardingCompletedAt is
        null (the floor — a fresh resident sees it). The gate is the owner-
        scope read of the profile field (the OnboardingViewModel.BannerEligible
        shape, D5), NEVER a claim (the thin-token rule, ADR 0001-B / D6).
      - Non-blocking (D5): it never gates sign-in. The [Authorize] on the
        walk-through is the standard signed-in gate; this banner is a plain
        affordance. The only way to clear it for real is the explicit
        finish/skip POST (D2/D4); the close button is a *client-side* dismiss
        only (the onboarding-banner.js module — a sessionStorage flag, never a
        write to OnboardingCompletedAt).
      - The copy is the closed onboarding.banner.* kw-l set (D7, the 15-key
        set U03 authored) — never an inline string (C-M22·6).
      - Signed-in residents only: an unauthenticated request has no subject,
        so there is no profile read and no banner (the LocaleController.
        BuildModel null-safe idiom).

    Dismissal is remembered per browser via sessionStorage (the pinned-
    announcement dismiss idiom, _PinnedAnnouncement.cshtml) — a plain ES
    module (tsc-built, no bundler), CSP-safe (script-src 'self').
*@
@using Kumunita.Core.UserInfo
@using Kumunita.Web.Security
@inject IUserInfoService UserInfo
@inject Kumunita.Core.Localization.ILocalizationService Localization
@inject Kumunita.Core.Localization.ITranslationProvider Translation
@inject Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.IHttpContextAccessor HttpContextAccessor
@{
    // Signed-in resident only: an unauthenticated request has no subject →
    // no profile read, no banner (the null-safe idiom, D5/D6).
    string? subject = User.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true
        ? KumunitaPrincipal.SubjectId(User)
        : null;
    // The owner-scope read (the profile field, never a claim — D6). A null
    // profile (a profile-less actor can't finish onboarding) yields no banner.
    Profile? profile = subject is null ? null : await UserInfo.GetProfileAsync(subject);

    // BannerEligible = the completion read is null (the floor, D5). Non-null
    // → the banner clears (the resident finished / skipped).
    bool bannerEligible = profile is not null && profile.OnboardingCompletedAt is null;
}
@if (bannerEligible)
{
    // The banner's accessible names are server-resolved (the kw-l TagHelper
    // can't wrap an attribute); the a11y.* floor is the closed set.
    var effLang = await EffectiveLanguageCode.ResolveAsync(HttpContextAccessor.HttpContext?.Request, Localization, Translation);
    string ariaRegion   = await Translation.GetAsync("a11y.onboarding_region", effLang);
    string ariaAction   = await Translation.GetAsync("a11y.onboarding_action", effLang);
    string ariaDismiss  = await Translation.GetAsync("a11y.onboarding_dismiss", effLang);

    <div class="kumunita-onboarding-banner alert alert-secondary alert-dismissible fade show mb-3"
         role="region" aria-label="@ariaRegion">
        <div class="container-fluid py-2 d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
            <span class="me-auto me-2">
                <kw-l key="onboarding.banner.text">Finish setting up your account?</kw-l>
            </span>
            <a class="btn btn-sm btn-primary text-nowrap" href="/onboarding"
               aria-label="@ariaAction"><kw-l key="onboarding.banner.action">Start setup</kw-l></a>
            <button type="button" class="btn-close"
                    data-dismiss-key="kumunita-onboarding-banner-dismissed"
                    aria-label="@ariaDismiss"></button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script type="module" src="~/js/lib/onboarding-banner.js"></script>
}
